# .gitignore — world/src/
#
# Template-owned; copier update keeps it current. Project-wide rules belong in the root .gitignore.
# No inline comments in this file: Git reads a # after a pattern as part of the pattern.

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Generated pronunciation audio
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Derived from each lexicon's IPA on request: regenerable, costly to make, and too large for
# plain Git. The rule sits here rather than inside languages/ because world/src/ ships with
# every fiction project. Turning the constructed-language kit off (or worldbuilding, which
# takes the kit with it) removes the template's files from languages/ but keeps your languages
# and their audio folders; this rule goes on keeping that audio out of Git.
languages/*/audio/
